Below is the **100-sub-issue implementation backlog for MarkHere**, derived directly from the 11 architecture documents. The sequence is dependency-aware: an issue should not bypass architectural work assigned to an earlier issue merely because a later feature can be made to “work” faster.

I also re-verified the architecture against current upstream guidance. Electron still recommends renderer sandboxing, context isolation, sender validation, restrictive navigation/CSP, careful `shell.openExternal` handling, and custom protocols instead of unrestricted `file://`. ([Electron][1]) CodeMirror 6 continues to use immutable state plus transactions, which fits MarkHere’s canonical revision model. ([CodeMirror][2]) CommonMark 0.31.2 remains the current published CommonMark specification. ([CommonMark Spec][3])

