# Issue 1 - Establish the MarkHere Repository, Toolchain, Architecture Boundaries, and Provenance

This issue creates the foundation on which every other MarkHere feature is built. No editor work, filesystem access, export functionality, or UI feature should be started until the repository has explicit package boundaries and development rules.

MarkHere is **not** a renamed MarkText fork. According to ADR-002, it is a distinct application that may selectively reuse/adapt suitable MarkText code. The monorepo must therefore make it obvious which code belongs to MarkHere, which packages are process-neutral, and which files contain inherited or adapted MarkText/Muya material.

The architecture defined by `01-system-overview.md`, `09-deployment-strategy.md`, `10-testing-strategy.md`, and ADR-001 through ADR-005 must be established here.

The expected conceptual structure is:

```text
markhere/
├─ apps/
│  └─ desktop/
├─ packages/
│  ├─ document-model/
│  ├─ markdown-engine/
│  ├─ wysiwyg-editor/
│  ├─ source-editor/
│  ├─ export-core/
│  ├─ ipc-contract/
│  ├─ shared/
│  └─ test-fixtures/
├─ build/
├─ docs/
├─ scripts/
├─ tests/
└─ package.json
```

Completion of Issue 1 means a developer can clone the repository, run one documented install command, run lint/typecheck/tests, start a minimal secure Electron window, and produce a development build without any hidden local-machine configuration.

## Issue 1.1 - Create the pnpm TypeScript Monorepo

Create the repository root and establish the pnpm workspace described by ADR-004.

Implementation tasks:

* Create the root `package.json`.
* Declare `packageManager` with an exact reviewed pnpm major/minor range.
* Add `pnpm-workspace.yaml`.
* Create `apps/desktop`.
* Create all process-neutral packages defined by the system overview.
* Give internal packages explicit names such as `@markhere/document-model`.
* Mark application-only packages private.
* Configure workspace dependencies using `workspace:*`.
* Do not introduce Lerna, Nx, Turborepo, or another orchestration framework unless a future ADR authorizes it.
* Add `.gitignore`, `.editorconfig`, `.npmrc`, and a root README.
* Do not place shared business logic directly in `apps/desktop`.

Package dependencies must follow the architectural dependency direction:

```text
desktop
  ↓
ipc-contract
  ↓
application services
  ↓
document-model / markdown-engine / export-core
```

Electron-specific modules must never become dependencies of `document-model`, Markdown parsing, export IR, or other process-neutral packages.

**Acceptance criteria**

* `pnpm install` succeeds from a clean checkout.
* `pnpm -r list` shows the expected packages.
* Each package can be typechecked independently.
* No circular workspace dependency exists.
* A dependency diagram can be generated without unexpected Electron dependencies in process-neutral packages.

**Traceability:** ADR-004, ADR-045, NFR-MNT-001.

